# This file is load-bearing for `flwr run`, not just for git.
#
# `flwr run` builds a FAB (Flower App Bundle) from this app directory. Its
# packager (flwr.cli.utils.filter_paths_for_publish) reads the .gitignore *in
# this directory* — it does NOT consult the repo-root .gitignore — and then
# rejects any bundled path deeper than MAX_DIR_DEPTH (10). `.venv/` contains
# vendored packages nested well past that (e.g.
# .venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/numpy-*.dist-info/licenses/numpy/_core/src/
# npysort/x86-simd-sort/LICENSE.md), so without the `.venv/` line below the FAB
# build fails with "exceeds the maximum directory depth of 10" before the run
# can start. Keep `.venv/` here.
.venv/
out/
.federation/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
